# The genuine regular-family fundamental group and its marked generators

The covering-space construction proves fibre injection, exactness of the
actual projection, splitting by the actual zero section, and agreement
of conjugation with actual transport. A proved free presentation of the
actual regular base then gives the lattice-by-free-group description.

Explicit semicircle lifts through the constructed half-triangle
uniformization identify a joint free basis whose true lattice action is
exactly `A₁`, `A₂`. The actual special period map supplies an unconditional
instance, retaining the native family topology and the original lattice.

The outer-meridian calculation concerns literal planar circles with
specified tails. Identifying their images in the assembled threefold
requires the separate actual attaching-map and van Kampen constructions;
no conclusion about the assembled threefold is assumed here.
